// The worker protocol. Workers call the leader scheduler; there are no calls the other way,
// so workers can sit behind NAT (a homelab node on Tailscale, a pod in Kubernetes).
//
// The heartbeat carries everything: the worker reports what it is running and what it has
// free, and the leader answers with new assignments and attempts to cancel. Reporting a
// running attempt renews its lease. A worker that stops heartbeating loses its leases, and
// its jobs are retried elsewhere.

